{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Lamport clocks: ordering without a clock",
  "hook": "How do Lamport clocks order events, and what can't they tell you?",
  "topic": "distributed/time/lamport-clocks",
  "tags": [
    "distributed",
    "clocks",
    "causality"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "series": "distributed-time-and-consistency",
  "series_index": 1,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "caption": "Each process keeps one integer; every message carries it.",
      "narration": "With no shared clock, each process keeps a single integer counter and stamps every message it sends.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Lamport clocks",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "rules",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Each process keeps a counter L",
            "Local event: L = L + 1",
            "Send: L = L + 1, attach L",
            "Receive: L = max(L, m.L) + 1"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "rules",
          "at": 3500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "On receive, the clock jumps past the sender's stamp.",
      "narration": "P1 sends a message stamped three. P2 was at one, so it takes the max, adds one, and moves to four.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Receive rule",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "p1",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "P1: L = 3",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 24,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "blue",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "P2: L = 1",
          "x": 54,
          "y": 24,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "m",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "p1",
          "to": "p2",
          "at": 1500,
          "enter": "draw",
          "label": "msg(L=3)"
        },
        {
          "id": "p2b",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "P2 after: L = 4",
          "x": 54,
          "y": 48,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 4000,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "u",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "p2",
          "to": "p2b",
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "draw",
          "label": "max(1,3)+1"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The receiver can never stay behind the stamp it just saw.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 68,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 6500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "caption": "If a happened before b, then L(a) < L(b).",
      "narration": "This gives the clock condition: whenever event a causally precedes event b, the first timestamp is strictly smaller.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "The guarantee",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "on send(m):\n  L = L + 1\n  m.L = L\non receive(m):\n  L = max(L, m.L) + 1",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "g",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "a -> b implies L(a) < L(b)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 3500,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "g",
          "at": 5000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "The converse fails: a smaller stamp does not mean \"caused\".",
      "narration": "But the reverse is false. Two events on different processes can have ordered stamps without any message linking them.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "What it cannot tell",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "e1",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "e1 on P1: L = 2",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "blue",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "e2",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "e2 on P3: L = 5",
          "x": 54,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 38,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "orange",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "x",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "L(e1) < L(e2), yet no message ever connected them.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 2500,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "red"
        },
        {
          "id": "y",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "L(a) < L(b) does NOT imply a -> b.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "y",
          "at": 6000,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "z",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Break ties with process id to get a total order.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 70,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 7500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "caption": "To detect concurrency you need more than one integer per event.",
      "narration": "Lamport clocks give a cheap total order, but cannot flag concurrent writes. That is what vector clocks add next.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Choosing a clock",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Total order, cheap: Lamport + process id",
            "Detect concurrent events: vector clocks",
            "Stay near wall time: hybrid logical clocks"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "l",
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "takeaway": "A Lamport clock yields an order consistent with causality, but a smaller timestamp never proves one event caused another.",
  "sources": [
    "https://lamport.azurewebsites.net/pubs/time-clocks.pdf"
  ]
